          "body": "The second `@pytest.mark.xfail(strict=True, reason=(\"DEFECT 2b ...\"))` decorator is not followed by a `def`. Instead the next token is another `@pytest.mark.xfail(...)` decorator, which is then followed by `def test_xfail_upsert_event_empty_content_is_reported_as_missing`. In Python, a decorator must be immediately followed by a function/class definition; a decorator followed by another decorator is a SyntaxError, so the whole module fails to import and none of the 800+ lines of tests run. Even if it parsed, the DEFECT 2b case would be silently dropped. Either attach a body to this decorator (e.g. a test asserting the 460/660 behaviour) or delete it, since the same defect is already covered by `test_xfail_world_read_gate_rejects_group_only_rows`.",
